# Infrastructure rules

- MVP local stack uses Docker Compose for PostgreSQL and Redis; apps may run locally or in containers as documented.
- Do not add Kubernetes, Kafka or service mesh in MVP.
- Environments: local, test, staging (when introduced), production.
- CI baseline: install -> lint -> typecheck -> test -> build.
- Migrations are applied deliberately during deploy; do not auto-destruct/recreate production DB.
- Use health/readiness endpoints for API/worker dependencies as needed.
- Structured logs use correlation IDs.
- Add Sentry/error tracking and metrics incrementally, but provider cost/usage observability is a first-class production concern.
- `.env.example` contains names and safe examples only, never secrets.
